      <div><p class="eyebrow">About</p><h1>Odunayo Ogundepo</h1><p class="dek">LLM Researcher and Applied Scientist.</p></div>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>I’m an Applied Scientist at Amazon working on Alexa Personalization. Part of my work focuses on helping Alexa learn useful information from a user’s interactions and apply the right user memories at the right moment.</p>
      <p>Before Amazon, I was a Senior Data Scientist at LexisNexis, where I worked on retrieval-augmented generation, conversational search, entity linking, and named entity recognition.</p>
      <p>I hold a Master’s degree in Computer Science from the University of Waterloo, supervised by Prof. Jimmy Lin. I’m deeply interested in improving NLP systems for African languages, and I collaborate on research and side projects with people across different companies and research communities.</p>
      <h2>Experience</h2>
      <p>My professional work spans applied science, personalization, retrieval-augmented generation, conversational search, entity linking, named entity recognition, data quality, and model evaluation.</p>
